index e90eb8f..3caeadd 100644
--- a/docs/drivers/adreno-metal.md
+++ b/docs/drivers/adreno-metal.md
@@ -48,3 +48,7 @@ With `sheng-gpu-trace=1`, kernel event 65 identifies the Metal device and comman
 `sheng-wallpaper-freeze=1` isolates wallpaper rendering. A Poster renderer retains its first successfully drawn and stored IOSurface output of at least two million pixels, then parks later command buffers before runtime submission. Parked buffers remain committed and unscheduled; their owners and queue leases stay retained. Previously submitted work completes normally. PosterBoard, backboardd and other clients continue submitting. The mode defaults to off.
 
 Detailed latency records identify slow encoder calls, callback invoke addresses and resource destruction. Kernel sampling of the render, encode and completion threads correlates upstream waits.
+
+Metal clients preserve requested sample counts. The iOS 18 integration retains IOSurface plane identity in texture views, uses the development translator and exposes a bounded per-process compilation budget through `M2V_PIPELINE_TURNS`. Unused owned backing can be released by the room worker with up to 512 MiB queued.
+
+For 22H384, `initLimits` fills the embedded Metal table's 2D texture dimensions from runtime capability queries. Tungsten's image importer and PhotosUICore consume that table through `limits`. The initializer validates the base object size and table address before writing the fields.
